The painted window is `[offset, offset + height)`. The dedupe in the plan computes:
- `paintedTop = wrapped.length - (historyNoSticky - sticky)`.

Note `plan.history = consumable + reserve` after `consumable -= sticky`. And `historyNoSticky = consumable + reserve` before subtracting sticky. So `plan.history = historyNoSticky - sticky` when sticky stays > 0. And if `sticky` is zeroed by the dedupe, `plan.history = historyNoSticky`. Good — so `paintedTop = wrapped.length - plan.history` in the pinned case, i.e., the window top when following.

